+### Fixed-panel tissue extension
+
+The post hoc tissue extension retained a frozen panel of TSHR and IGF1R in five standard-release GTEx v8 tissues. QTL sample counts were 574 (thyroid), 483 (cultured fibroblasts), 581 (subcutaneous adipose), 469 (visceral adipose) and 670 (whole blood). The original v8 archive supplied significant variant–gene pairs and eGenes records for all tested genes; gene-specific release thresholds exceeded 5×10⁻⁸ for every eligible combination, permitting complete selection at the fixed threshold. Absence from the tested-gene file was distinguished from a minimum eQTL P value above the threshold. The standard release includes multiple ancestries; the overall donor cohort was 85.3% European American, not a tissue-specific percentage.
+
+Variants were restricted to ±1 Mb of the source GENCODE v26 TSS, P < 5×10⁻⁸, F > 10 and MAF ≥ 0.01. GTEx variant IDs identify GRCh38 REF and ALT, with slope referring to ALT. Actual effect-allele frequencies were reconstructed from each selected eGene MAF and ref_factor, not by treating MAF as ALT frequency. GTEx mappings linked GRCh38 variants to rsIDs and GRCh37 reference coordinates. PLINK clumping used 503 European reference samples, r² < 0.001 and a 10-Mb window; an independent genotype-based calculation reproduced selection. One of 20 thyroid IGF1R candidates was absent from the reference, while its strongest candidate was retained. All selected variants were non-palindromic and matched exactly in the five disease datasets; no proxies or relaxed thresholds were used.
+
+Each of the four estimable gene–tissue combinations retained one SNP. Wald estimates used βY/βX and SEY/|βX| with normal two-sided P values and 95% CIs; independent R calculations verified all 20 estimates. The UKB linear-to-log-odds conversion was applied once. ORs represent one unit of inverse-normal-transformed normalized expression; they are not directly comparable to an intervention or to the reconstructed eQTLGen scale. Primary adjusted P = min(1,10P) for FinnGen GD; secondary adjusted P = min(1,40P) for the other datasets. The 30 unestimable cells remained in the planned families. Single-instrument analyses cannot support heterogeneity, leave-one-out or MR-Egger diagnostics. Significant-only eQTL pairs were not used for colocalization; full regional data were not obtained from the requester-pays resource, and no tissue posterior was calculated. Tissue_extension in the single Supplementary Dataset retains all 50 cells, availability, selected and excluded candidates, harmonized alleles and source statistics.
 
